---- Client environment (Vite) ----
Copy this file to `.env.local` for local development, or set the same keys in
your hosting provider's dashboard (e.g. Vercel -> Settings -> Environment
Variables) before the production build.

Base URL of the API server.
Dev: leave UNSET — the Vite proxy forwards /api to :5000.
Prod: set this when the client and server are on different origins
      (e.g. Vercel frontend + Vercel backend).
VITE_API_URL=https://e-project-server.vercel.app/api

Base URL of a real-time Socket.IO server (same host as VITE_API_URL, WITHOUT
/api). LEAVE THIS UNSET on Vercel: serverless hosting has no WebSocket server,
so the client automatically falls back to polling (~5s) instead.
Set it only when you deploy the backend on a host that supports WebSockets
(Render, Koyeb, Railway).
# VITE_SOCKET_URL=https://your-long-running-backend.example.com

# Stripe keys belong in the backend environment. The frontend fetches the
# publishable key from GET /api/payments/config; never put the secret key here.
# Backend: STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_... and STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...
